d enhances bacterial cytotoxicity. <source>Microb. Pathog.</source> <volume>33</volume>:<fpage>135</fpage>&#x02013;143.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12220990</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Gassama-Diagne, A., W. Yu, M. ter Beest, F. Martin-Belmonte, A. Kierbel, J. Engel, and K. Mostov. <year>2006</year>. Phosphatidylinositol-3,4,5-trisphosphate regulates the formation of the basolateral plasma membrane in epithelial cells. <source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>8</volume>:<fpage>963</fpage>&#x02013;970.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16921364</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Geiser, T., B. Kazmierczak, L. Garrity-Ryan, M. Matthay, and J. Engel. <year>2001</year>. <italic>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</italic> ExoT inhibits in vitro lung epithelial wound repair. <source>Cell. Microbiol.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>223</fpage>&#x02013;236.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11298646</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Gibson, M.C., and N. Perrimon. <year>2003</year>. Apicobasal polarization: epithelial form and function. <source>Curr. Opin. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>15</volume>:<fpage>747</fpage>&#x02013;752.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14644201</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Hansen, S.H., A. Olsson, and J.E. Casanova. <year>1995</year>. Wortmannin, an inhibitor of phosphoinositide 3-kinase, inhibits transcytosis in polarized epithelial cells. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>270</volume>:<fpage>28425</fpage>&#x02013;28432.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7499348</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Kazmierczak, B., K. Mostov, and J. Engel. <year>2001</year>. Interaction of bacterial pathogens with polarized epithelium. <source>Annu. Rev. Microbiol.</source> <volume>55</volume>:<fpage>407</fpage>&#x02013;435.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11544362</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Kazmierczak, B.I., K. Mostov, and J.N. Engel. <year>2004</year>. Epithelial cell polarity alters Rho-GTPase responses to <italic>Pseudomonas aeruginosa.</italic> <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>15</volume>:<fpage>411</fpage>&#x02013;419.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14595106</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Kierbel, A., A. Gassama-Diagne, K. Mostov, and J.N. Engel. <year>2005</year>. The phosphoinositol-3-kinase-protein kinase B/Akt pathway is critical for <italic>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</italic> strain PAK internalization. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>2577</fpage>&#x02013;2585.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15772151</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Klarlund, J.K., A. Guilherme, J.J. Holik, J.V. Virbasius, A. Chawla, and M.P. Czech. <year>1997</year>. Signaling by phosphoinositide-3,4,5-trisphosphate through proteins containing pleckstrin and Sec7 homology domains. <source>Science.</source> <volume>275</volume>:<fpage>1927</fpage>&#x02013;1930.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9072969</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Klarlund, J.K., L.E. Rameh, L.C. Cantley, J.M. Buxton, J.J. Holik, C. Sakelis, V. Patki, S. Corvera, and M.P. Czech. <year>1998</year>. Regulation of GRP1-catalyzed ADP ribosylation factor guanine nucleotide exchange by phosphatidylinositol 3,4,5-trisphosphate. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>273</volume>:<fpage>1859</fpage>&#x02013;1862.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9442017</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="other">Lipschutz, J.H., L.E. O'Brien, Y. Altschuler, D. Avrahami, Y. Nguyen, K. Tang, and K.E. Mostov. <year>2001</year>. Analysis of membrane traffic in polarized epithelial cells. <italic>In</italic> Current Protocols in Cell Biology. John Wiley &#x00026; Sons Inc., New York.</citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="other">Mandell, G.L., J.E. Bennett, and R. Dolin. <year>2000</year>. Mandell, Douglas, and Bennett's Principles and Practice of Infectious Diseases. Churchill Livingstone, Philadelphia.</citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Pier, G.B., M. Grout, and T.S. Zaidi. <year>1997</year>. Cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator is an epithelial cell receptor for clearance of <italic>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</italic> from the lung. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>94</volume>:<fpage>12088</fpage>&#x02013;12093.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9342367</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Pinal, N., D.C. Goberdhan, L. Collinson, Y. Fujita, I.M. Cox, C. Wilson, and F. Pichaud. <year>2006</year>. Regulated and polarized PtdIns(3,4,5)P3 accumulation is essential for apical membrane morphogenesis in photoreceptor epithelial cells. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>140</fpage>&#x02013;149.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16431366</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Pizarro-Cerda, J., and P. Cossart. <year>2004</year>. Subversion of phosphoinositide metabolism by intracellular bacterial pathogens. <source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>6</volume>:<fpage>1026</fpage>&#x02013;1033.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15516995</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Pollard, T.D., and G.G. Borisy. <year>2003</year>. Cellular motility driven by assembly and disassembly of actin filaments. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>112</volume>:<fpage>453</fpage>&#x02013;465.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12600310</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Sadoul, K., J. Lang, C. Montecucco, U. Weller, R. Regazzi, S. Catsicas, C.B. Wollheim, and P.A. Halban. <year>1995</year>. SNAP-25 is expressed in islets of Langerhans and is involved in insulin release. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>128</volume>:<fpage>1019</fpage>&#x02013;1028.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7896868</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Vanhaesebroeck, B., and D.R. Alessi. <year>2000</year>. The PI3K-PDK1 connection: more than just a road to PKB. <source>Biochem. J.</source> <volume>346</volume>:<fpage>561</fpage>&#x02013;576.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10698680</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">von Stein, W., A. Ramrath, A. Grimm, M. Muller-Borg, and A. Wodarz. <year>2005</year>. Direct association of Bazooka/PAR-3 with the lipid phosphatase PTEN reveals a link between the PAR/aPKC complex and phosphoinositide signaling. <source>Development.</source> <volume>132</volume>:<fpage>1675</fpage>&#x02013;1686.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15743877</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Watton, S.J., and J. Downward. <year>1999</year>. Akt/PKB localisation and 3&#x02032; phosphoinositide generation at sites of epithelial cell-matrix and cell-cell interaction. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>9</volume>:<fpage>433</fpage>&#x02013;436.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10226029</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Wymann, M.P., M. Zvelebil, and M. Laffargue. <year>2003</year>. Phosphoinositide 3-kinase signalling&#x02013;which way to target? <source>Trends Pharmacol. Sci.</source> <volume>24</volume>:<fpage>366</fpage>&#x02013;376.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12871670</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Yu, W., L.E. O'Brien, F. Wang, H. Bourne, K.E. Mostov, and M.M. Zegers. <year>2003</year>. Hepatocyte growth factor switches orientation of polarity and mode of movement during morphogenesis of multicellular epithelial structures. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>748</fpage>&#x02013;763.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12589067</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal">Yu, W., A. Datta, P. Leroy, L.E. O'Brien, G. Mak, T.S. Jou, K.S. Matlin, K.E. Mostov, and M.M. Zegers. <year>2005</year>. Beta1-integrin orients epithelial polarity via Rac1 and laminin. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>433</fpage>&#x02013;445.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15574881</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>